# =============================================================================
# THE CONTROL for gridpro_quilt.dat: section 27's straightened C/H, at the split
# that matches the quilt's cell count -- 8640 cells against 8664, a 0.3% match.
#
# Section 29. Section 27f is why this file exists: at 21600 cells against 29120
# the straightened C/H read as 3-6x WORSE in the solve, and matching the count
# turned that into 1.7-2.4x better. A gate-2 comparison across different cell
# counts measures the count.
#
#   python3 docs/research/gridpro-blocking-method/make_ch.py \
#       --layers 2 --split 12 --turn-blend 0.8 --wake 8 \
#       --out gridpro_quilt_control.json
#   ./run.sh -conf docs/research/gridpro-blocking-method/gridpro_quilt_control.dat
#
# It is NOT gridpro_ch_straight.dat: that one is --split 32 and 28640 cells, and
# section 27 ships it as the defensible default. This is the same topology
# coarsened to be comparable with a 54-block radial fan.
#
# A RESEARCH HARNESS, not a shipped case.
# =============================================================================

MESH_MODE 1
MESH_TOPOLOGY_FILE docs/research/gridpro-blocking-method/gridpro_quilt_control.json

# The aerofoil the C-grid case already ships: two segments, upper and lower,
# split at the leading edge because that is where a block corner sits. There is
# NO far-field geometry -- the rectangle is declared, corner by corner.
GEOM_FILE examples/geometries/naca0012_cgrid.dat

BL_INITIAL_THICKNESS 0.001
MB_SPLIT_QUADS 1

# The FALLBACK, and here it is load bearing: the far-field and outlet edges
# carry no binding, so this is where their condition comes from. The aerofoil's
# sides are bound and take 'wall' off their own sidecar. A real case would want
# inlet / outlet / farfield told apart, which needs a far-field geometry file.
BC_GEOM farfield

# The repo default of 20 sweeps DIVERGES on this family (section 8g); five is
# where the wall height is held and nothing has turned.
MB_SMOOTH_ITERS 5

EXPORT_VTK 1
OUTPUT_FILENAME results/meshes/gridpro_quilt_control/mesh_gridpro_quilt_control.vtk
